578:
It shall be unlawful for any person:
(1) To deposit, throw, place, or cause to be deposited, thrown or placed, into or upon any public square, street, alley or sidewalk of the city, or the private property of another any paper, rag, shavings, trash, or rubbish; any chips, ashes, or cuttings of vines, shrubbery, or trees; any filth, offal, or rotten fruit, vegetable, or meat; any dead birds or animals; any human or other excrement or wastes; or any liquids or any other thing or things which are or may become offensive, or which may injure or damage any of the public squares, streets, alleys, or sidewalks of the city, or the private property of another, or interfere with the free use and enjoyment of same;
(2) To erect a dam or other obstruction or prevent the natural flow of water, causing it to collect in pools upon any public square, street, alley or sidewalk of the city, or the private property of another; to allow any such dam or obstruction to continue on any property owned or controlled by such person, after knowledge of its existence; or to do or cause to be done any work the effect of which will be to dam, obstruct, or prevent the natural flow of water, causing it to collect in pools upon any public square, street, alley or sidewalk of the city, or the private property of another;
(3) To knowingly dispose of waste or rubbish directly into an open or flowing body of water; or
(4) To cause or allow the erosion of soil from water or wind or the movement of sediments into state waters or onto any public square, street, alley or sidewalk of the city, or the private property of another, unless pursuant to and in compliance with a permit issued under article III of this chapter.
(Code 1975, § 9-4; Res. No. 2-2006, 1-3-06)

